        <detaileddescription>
<para>Class Constructor. The jobs include:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Initialise sample buffers <simplesect kind="see"><para>init_sample_buffers()</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Create an instance of <ref refid="classBladerfDevice" kindref="compound">BladerfDevice</ref>, and set it to use on TX and two RXs</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Provide frequency plan to the device to enable quick tune functionality <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>start_freq</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The start frequency of the frequency plan </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>num_steps</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of frequency steps </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>step_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The interval between two consecutive frequencies </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>samp_rate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Sampling rate </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rx_gain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The gain of the radar RX channel </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>tx_gain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The gain of the radar TX channel </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ref_gain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The gain of the reference TX and RX channel </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>enable_biastee</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Set the flag if BT-100 and BT-200 are connected with radar TX and radar RX channels </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>burst_len</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of samples per pulse </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>recv_buf_len</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of samples to receive from one RX channel. Prefer to be bigger than burst_len </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>num_buffers</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of buffers to use in the underlying data stream </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>buffer_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The size of the underlying steam buffers, in samples. Must be a multiple of 1024. Samples are only transferred when a buffer of this size is filled. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>num_transfers</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The number of active USB transfers that may be in-flight at any given time </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>pulse_amplitude</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The amplitude of the transmitted pulse </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>cw_frequency</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The baseband frequency of the single tone pulse </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>isChirp</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Set this when using chirp waveform </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>chirp_bandwidth</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bandiwdth of chirp </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ts_inc_send</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>After each frequency tunning, wait ts_inc_send ms before transmitting radar pulse and receiving radar echo. Note that the value depends on the processing power and the USB overhead of the host computer. It is recommand to be larger than 1. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
